Concept:
I was thinking about how to simplify my previous idea when I came across Satie's Embryons desséchés: No. 1, D'Holothurie.
The whole work is called Dried Embryos, and the first movement is about a sea cucumber.
I was reading the original music sheet and found a lot of funny notes and descriptions written by him. 
hey almost seem like casual observations about a sea cucumber's daily life.
https://imslp.org/images/3/3a/TN-Satie%2C_Erik-Klavierwerke_Peters_Klemm_Band_2_03_Embryons_desseches.jpg 

So I decided to combine the idea of "drying" with the title of the piece and use a sea cucumber as my main character. It gradually shrinks throughout the day.

I found the music quite whimsical and playful
So I used colorful dots that change color every second to match that.
